      "writtenOn": "2022-02-23T14:13:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e will this cause a call to AudioManager.handleBluetoothActiveDeviceChanged() indicating the new codec?\nThis setCodecConfigPreference() tries to apply the codec config to both local source and remote sink, and it doesn\u0027t invoke that Audio API directly. It depends on whether there is any codec different after applying the requested config.\n\n\u003e This is important to know because the audio framework would have to minimise disruption in case the codec change does not cause a reconfiguration of the audio path from SW encoder to HW offload encoder\nThis would be a bit hard to achieve, but is depended on encoders capabilities. If you change from a SW only to SW + HW encoders, the BT stack will select the HW first, or vice versa. If you don\u0027t want to have a datapath change, you have to prevent from such config switching.",
      "parentUuid": "31e22bf4_77ad08c4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 897,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 897,
        "endChar": 81
      },
      "revId": "dd21af4e22fc956c8bf36862deed19505cb30546",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
